    <!--
      Korean. Machine translation, reviewed for consistency of terminology.

      Two things in here are load-bearing rather than cosmetic:

      * The help page's menu paths have to name screens exactly as those screens are
        named in this file. A path pointing at a heading that does not exist in Korean is
        worse than one left in English.
      * The short strings used for bolding (help_name_*, notif_name_*,
        settings_to_hide_name_shizuku_hide) are matched as substrings inside the longer
        strings they highlight. Word them differently in the two places and the bolding
        silently does nothing. In Korean this means the particle goes after the phrase,
        never inside it.
    -->
